description "Trivalent, secureblue's hardened Chromium fork"

supports "fedora"

requires "build-environment"
requires "display-manager"
requires "selinux-policy"

// `trivalent-selinux`'s policy module requires `flatpak_home_t`, which
// `flatpak-selinux` defines and `flatpak` pulls in, so `semodule -i` in its
// `%post` cannot resolve without flatpak already in the image. Measured
// 2026-09-06 on `quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44`: installing the rpm alone
// gives *"Failed to resolve typeattributeset statement at .../trivalent/cil:58"*,
// and the same rpm over a layer carrying `flatpak` loads the module.
//
// This is an ordering the module never declared and got for free: while it was
// `trivalent` it sorted after `flatpak` on the tie-break, and renaming it
// `browsers/trivalent` put it in front. That is what turned the fedora leg red
// on 2026-09-05, not the `-447128` to `-447136` move it looked like — those two
// builds are the same noarch package built once per architecture, byte
// identical in payload, scriptlets and requires, so no pin reaches this.
requires "flatpak"

packages "trivalent" "trivalent-qt6-ui" "trivalent-selinux" enablerepo="secureblue"
